---
import { withBase } from '../../data/site';
import { UI, t, type Lang } from '../../data/i18n';
import { PROJECTS } from '../../data/projects';
import { WORK } from '../../data/work';

const { lang } = Astro.props;
const ui = UI[lang];

// 卡片角落的字母标（代替 damon 的产品 logo）
const markOf = (name: string) => name.trim().charAt(0).toUpperCase();
const isLive = (statusZh: string) => statusZh === '开发中';
---

<section class="about">
  <h2 class="section-h">{ui.aboutTitle}</h2>
  {
    lang === 'zh' ? (
      <>
        <p>
          这几年一直在 AI 创业公司做产品。工作后才发现，那些本来不值得人持续投入注意力、却不得不处理的事情，反而持续占用人的时间。于是我正在做
          <em>Origin</em>
          这款产品，替人安排运动和饮食，追踪日常花销，和处理工作上的任务。
        </p>
        <p>
          打磨 <em>Origin</em>
          时，原本只想把精力放在产品本身，却不断需要反复与编程 agent
          沟通、排错。这件事让我产生了做第二款产品 <em>Craft</em>
          的冲动，让人把注意力花在做什么、为什么做、做出来的是不是自己想要的结果上。
        </p>
        <p>
          过去几次创业在没有正反馈的情况下，公司会安排人处理更多任务。这种现象也让我意识到，当一个组织无法降低方向上的不确定性时，很容易转而增加执行上的确定性。这些经历让我长期关注一个问题：什么样的组织环境能让人愿意投入、敢于判断、能够创造？
        </p>
        <p>
          我非常喜欢阅读，他人的文字让我敢于离开不喜欢的工作环境，更主动寻找真正想做的事情。也让我意识到钱可以让我对不喜欢的事情说&ldquo;不&rdquo;。生活中总有让我困惑和好奇的问题，于是我通过写作把模糊的东西想清楚，也许我的视角也能给正在阅读的你多一个参考。
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <p>
          These past few years I've been building products at AI startups. Once I started working,
          I noticed something: the things that don't deserve anyone's attention — yet still have to
          be dealt with — are exactly the ones that keep taking up our time. So I'm building{' '}
          <em>Origin</em>, a product that arranges your exercise and meals, tracks your daily
          spending, and handles your work tasks.
        </p>
        <p>
          While polishing <em>Origin</em>, I meant to focus on the product itself, but kept getting
          pulled into back-and-forths with coding agents, debugging. That experience gave me the
          urge to build a second product, <em>Craft</em> — one that lets people spend their
          attention on what to do, why to do it, and whether what gets built is actually what they
          want.
        </p>
        <p>
          In my past startups, when positive feedback was missing, the company would respond by
          assigning people more tasks. It made me realize: when an organization can't reduce
          uncertainty about direction, it tends to increase certainty about execution instead.
          These experiences left me with a question I keep coming back to: what kind of environment
          makes people willing to commit, brave enough to judge, and able to create?
        </p>
        <p>
          I love reading. Other people's words gave me the courage to leave work environments I
          didn't like and go look for what I truly wanted to do. They also made me see that money
          lets me say &ldquo;no&rdquo; to what I dislike. Life is full of questions that puzzle and
          intrigue me, so I write to think the vague ones through — and maybe my perspective can
          offer you, the reader, one more reference.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="section-h">{ui.portfolioTitle}</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    {
      PROJECTS.map((p) => (
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <h3 class="card-title">
              <span class="card-mark" style={`--mark:${p.accent}`} aria-hidden="true">{markOf(p.name)}</span>
              {p.links && p.links.length > 0 ? (
                <a href={p.links[0].href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{p.name}</a>
              ) : (
                <span>{p.name}</span>
              )}
              {isLive(t(p.status, 'zh')) && <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true" />}
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="card-tag">{t(p.tagline, lang)}</p>
          <p class="card-desc">{t(p.description, lang)}</p>
          {p.links && p.links.length > 0 && (
            <p class="card-links">
              {p.links.map((l, i) => (
                <>
                  {i > 0 && ' · '}
                  <a href={l.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{l.label}</a>
                </>
              ))}
            </p>
          )}
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="section-h">{ui.workTitle}</h2>
  <ol class="work-fold">
    {
      WORK.map((item) => (
        <li>
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="wf-logo">
                <img src={withBase(item.logo)} alt="" width="18" height="18" loading="lazy" />
              </span>
              <span class="wf-main">
                <span class="wf-role">{t(item.role, lang)}</span>
                {item.href ? (
                  <a class="wf-org" href={item.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    {t(item.org, lang)}
                  </a>
                ) : (
                  <span class="wf-org">{t(item.org, lang)}</span>
                )}
              </span>
              <span class="wf-period">
                {item.current && <span class="now" aria-hidden="true" />}
                {item.period.split(' — ')[0]}
                {item.current ? '' : ` — ${item.period.split(' — ')[1] ?? ''}`}
              </span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none">
                  <path d="M2.5 3.5L5 6l2.5-2.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="wf-body">
              <p class="wf-summary">{t(item.summary, lang)}</p>
              {item.highlights.length > 0 && (
                <ul class="points">
                  {item.highlights.map((h) => (
                    <li>{t(h, lang)}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              )}
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</section>
